  "facts": [
    "The Hangzhou Bay Bridge, spanning 35.7 km, cut the highway distance between Ningbo and Shanghai from 400 km to 180 km, slashing travel time from four hours to just two.",
    "Constructed with steel piles instead of concrete, the bridge’s foundations resist the bay’s 25‑foot tidal waves and corrosive saltwater, a first for such a long cable‑stayed structure.",
    "A 145.6‑meter lookout tower on the bridge’s mid‑span service centre offers tourists a panoramic view, while the centre itself survived a 2010 fire and reopened in December of that year."
